/// Fulfilment states an order moves through. Order here is narrative, not
/// enforced — `allowedOrderTransitions` in order.service.ts is the guard, and
/// it is the only thing that decides what may follow what.
///
/// PACKED sits between PROCESSING and SHIPPED: picked and boxed, but still on
/// the premises. That last part is why it belongs in
/// RESTOCKABLE_ON_CANCEL_STATUSES — cancelling a packed parcel must credit its
/// stock back, because nobody has it yet.
enum OrderStatus {
  PENDING
  CONFIRMED
  PROCESSING
  PACKED
  SHIPPED
  DELIVERED
  CANCELLED
  COMPLETED
}

/// How the CUSTOMER reached the shop — not how the order was entered.
///
/// WEBSITE means the shopper placed it themselves through the storefront, and
/// is the default because it is true of every order placed before this existed.
/// The rest are conversations a seller turned into an order by hand; which
/// staff member did that is `Order.createdByUserId`, and the ABSENCE of one is
/// what says the customer placed it themselves. The two fields answer different
/// questions and a manual order needs both.
///
/// There is deliberately no LANDING_PAGE member, and adding one later would be
/// a mistake. `Order.landingPageId` already records campaign attribution, and
/// two independently-written fields answering one question is exactly how the
/// two come to disagree with no way to tell which is right. A landing-page
/// order reads WEBSITE — which is true, it came through the storefront — and
/// carries its campaign on `landingPageId`.
/// See add-manual-orders-and-item-images design.md, Decision 6.
enum OrderChannel {
  WEBSITE
  WHATSAPP
  MESSENGER
  PHONE
  IN_STORE
  OTHER
}

